<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mfengu</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Fingo, amaMfengu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mfengu are a Xhosa-speaking people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-cape">Eastern Cape</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, formed largely from refugees who fled into Xhosa lands from the wars of the 1820s in Natal. Many allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a>, which settled them on land taken from the Xhosa from 1835 and used them as soldiers in its frontier wars. Their early adoption of mission education made them prominent among the region's African professionals.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mfengu.jpg" alt="Mfengu" width="217" height="260" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Captain_Veldtman_Bikitsha_-_Cape_Colony_Military_leader.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
